recommendations.recommendation:
Static, cacheable system prompt: role, invariants with reasons, workflow, markup grammar, modeling conventions. Per-run JSON bundle in the first user message (or after SYSTEM_PROMPT_DYNAMIC_BOUNDARY):
- action;
- target {id, type, natural_name verbatim, status, decl};
- selected_assumptions [{id, natural_name, rationale, status, decl}];
- model_index (all nodes, compact: id, type, natural_name, decl, has_lean, proved);
- vocabulary (from the audit: decl, type, short doc, file);
- relevant + global DECISION records;
- files {write_new_declarations_to, root_module};
- budgets {check_lean_calls, question_batches, questions_per_batch}.
The agent Reads/Greps the shadow for full Lean source. Pass prompts with verbatimPrompts:true.

Shadow at <globalStorage>/runs/<runId>/ws:
- copy *.lean, lakefile.*, lean-toolchain, lake-manifest.json;
- `cp -a --reflink=auto .lake/build` (preserving mtimes avoids rebuilds; verified);
- symlink .lake/packages (verified untouched) and bind it read-only in the sandbox;
- git init + base commit inside the shadow, so diffs come from `git diff base` and each feedback iteration is a commit.
Run EVERY Lean invocation on agent code under: bwrap --ro-bind / / --dev /dev --proc /proc --tmpfs /tmp --tmpfs $HOME --ro-bind $HOME/.elan $HOME/.elan --bind $SHADOW $SHADOW --ro-bind $REAL/.lake/packages $REAL/.lake/packages --chdir $SHADOW --unshare-all --die-with-parent --new-session --setenv HOME $HOME --setenv PATH $HOME/.elan/bin:/usr/bin:/bin lake build. Add memory and time limits (e.g. systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=4G). Fail closed if bwrap is missing, unless the user explicitly opts into unsafe mode.
